# The desktop build is made on Windows and the web app is deployed on Linux,
# so the same files are edited from both. Without this, whichever side commits
# next rewrites every line of a file it did not otherwise change, and a real
# one-line fix arrives as a 400-line diff nobody can review.
#
# `text=auto` stores LF in the repository and checks out whatever the platform
# uses, so nothing about editing on Windows changes.
* text=auto

# Executed by a shell, which will not accept CRLF in a shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Read by the container, where CRLF in a RUN line is a syntax error.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf

# Not text, whatever the heuristic decides: the card database is sqlite, and
# a normalised byte in it is a corrupted one.
*.sqlite binary
*.parquet binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
